## Frontend (FSD-aware)

- Colocate tests with the slice: `features/cancel-order/ui/CancelOrderButton.test.tsx`.
- Test through the **public API** (`index.ts`) where practical; test `model` logic (pure functions, hooks) directly and `ui` through user-level interactions (`@testing-library/user-event`).
- The generated repo ships Vitest + Testing Library only. Add a network-mocking layer (MSW or `openapi-fetch` middleware) at the `shared/api` boundary when the first test needs it, typed with the generated OpenAPI types so mocks cannot drift from the contract.
- Query by role/label (what users perceive), not by test IDs or class names.
- Don't test `shared/ui` primitives exhaustively; test their accessibility contract (roles, keyboard) once.
- `{{ fsd_lint_command }}` and `eslint` run in CI and in the pre-commit hook; a layer or slice violation fails both.
{%- endif %}
